event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":536,"item_id":"fc_0bfe6e1fa8f24ccf016adb3c6dea308191ae4e43b8ec87226b","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"base_candidate\\\":16,\\\"patches\\\":[{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/inputs\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"N001\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"M004\\\",\\\"M005\\\",\\\"M006\\\",\\\"M008\\\",\\\"M009\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/argument/0/uses\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"N001\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"M004\\\",\\\"M005\\\",\\\"M006\\\",\\\"M008\\\",\\\"M009\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Let J=[r/2,3r/2] and take compact C from H003. M005 gives compact C×J. The continuous e_t is bounded there by K and vanishes outside C. C is measurable and has finite Lebesgue measure. M008 gives integrability on C of the constant function K; M009 then gives integrability on ℝⁿ of b=K·1_C. For F(τ)(x)=e(x,τ) and F′(τ)(x)=e_t(x,τ), every F(τ) is strongly measurable by continuity, F(r) integrable by N001, and F′(r) strongly measurable. Smoothness gives the pointwise derivative in τ, and |F′(τ)(x)|≤b(x) for τ∈J. M006 therefore applies and gives E differentiable at r with derivative ∫e_t(x,r)dx. This proves N002 for arbitrary r.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"remove\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/applications/3\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"add\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/applications/-\\\",\\\"value\\\":{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M008\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"α=ℝⁿ, s=C, μ=Lebesgue, C-source constant=K.\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"C is measurable because compact subsets of Euclidean space are closed.\\\",\\\"Lebesgue measure of compact C is finite.\\\",\\\"K is a finite nonnegative real, so its extended norm is finite.\\\"]}},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"add\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/applications/-\\\",\\\"value\\\":{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M009\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"α=ℝⁿ, s=C, μ=Lebesgue, f(x)=K.\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"The constant K is integrable on C by M008.\\\",\\\"C is measurable because it is compact in Euclidean space.\\\"]}}]}\"}"}

